\* SIFI: Sci-Fi Plot Generator\* Last Modified: 8 July 1990 by wiml@milton.u.washington.edu\*\* Originally coded by Kevin D. Quitt (demott!kdq, kdq@demott.com)\* who commented, in the C version,\* "This program was converted on [24-July-1990] from a spaghetti-\* coded BASIC program (that almost worked). I am the original\* author of both works, though G*d only knows why someone would\* claim otherwise. .... Note that the original flowchart for this\* program is *not* my [kdq's] creation - I believe Gahan Wilson did it\* originally, I think about '81, published in OMNI magazine."\* Minor modifications to the C code by chad@anasaz.UUCP on 31 July 1990.\* Converted to spewfile format 7 August 1990 by wiml@milton.u.washington.edu,\* also a few more phrases added and probabilities tweaked.\* The \PRUNE pseudo-class is unique to the version of SPEW modified\* for this rulesfile.%SIZEtinygiantmicroscopicplanet-sizedhumongousitty-bitty%BEINGbugs, whichreptiles, whichmechanical devices, whichsuper persons, whoicky things, whichbeings composed completely of energy, which%BEINGTYPEextra-galacticMartianMoonBetelgeusian%COMETRESULTSdestroyed.saved by Jesus and the J.D.L.not destroyed, but everybody dies.saved by a a reclusive hermit and his cute alien pet.%KILLEDBYthe Atomic Bomba crowd of peasnts with torchesthe Army, Navy, Air Force, Marine Corps and/or Coast Guardorbiting laser satellitesguerilla foces%BUTthey fall in love with a beautiful girla cute little kid convinces them that people are OKa priest talks to them of GodCaptain Kirk uses logic on them%TERM1and they die. \PRUNEand they leave. \PRUNEand they turn into disgusting lumps. \PRUNE%TERM2but they die from catching chicken pox. \PRUNEso they kill us. \PRUNEso they put us under a benign dictatorship. \PRUNEso they eat us. \PRUNE%WEAPONRESULTSwhich failswhich kills them. \PRUNEwhich turns them into disgusting lumps. \PRUNE%DESCRIBEBEING\SIZE \BEINGTYPE \BEING \DESCRIBEBEINGTAIL%DESCRIBEBEINGTAILwant our women,want our women, take a few and leave. \PRUNEare friendly. \PRUNEare friendly, but misunderstood,misunderstand usunderstand us too wellare emissaries from Godlook upon us only as a source of nourishmentlook upon us only as a source of nourishment, and eat us. \PRUNE%DOBUT, but \BUT \TERM1%SIFI!(2)Earth is struck by a giant comet and \COMETRESULTS(5)Scientists discover or invent \DESCRIBEBEINGCURIE(5)Earth is attacked by \DESCRIBEBEINGCURIEEarth burns up or freezes or falls into the sun and everybody dies.Earth burns up or freezes or falls into the sun and almost everybody dies.%MAYBE(1)(1) not%DESCRIBEBEINGCURIE\DESCRIBEBEING and are\MAYBE radioactive, and can\MAYBE be killed by \KILLEDBY/ \WHATTODO%WHATTODO   \* WHATTODO is a recursive version of the iterative original\DOBUT \TERM2\DOBUT so scientists invent a weapon \WEAPONRESULTS \WHATTODO%MAIN\SIFI!/ \!\!%%